# Vendored subset of llama.cpp common/ — HEADERS ONLY
# Upstream: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
# Pinned commit: 687e7789271ec1276e3470f158428e11a4f80b6f
# Released upstream as llama.cpp b10330
#
# Implementations live in libllama-common.dylib, which
# scripts/provision-llama.sh stages into `.llama/b<release>/lib/` from the
# upstream release asset. We vendor only the headers needed to consume the
# chat/template/PEG API from CLlamaBridge.cpp. They must come from the exact
# commit recorded above so the C++ ABI matches that dylib.
#
# These headers are on the compiler's header search path directly, via
# `.headerSearchPath("third_party/llama_cpp_common")` in local-llm/Package.swift,
# because CLlamaBridge.cpp includes them ("chat.h" and friends). The llama.cpp
# and ggml *public* headers that these in turn include are vendored separately
# at local-llm/third_party/llama_cpp_api/ and reach the compiler a different
# way — see that directory's COMMIT for why. Both sets must come from the
# commit above, and both must match the staged dylibs: the mangled C++ symbol
# names do not change across these bumps, so a mismatch fails as silent runtime
# corruption rather than as a link error.
#
# The version is NOT whatever Homebrew happens to have installed. Homebrew is
# no longer involved in resolving llama.cpp — see local-llm/LLAMA_CPP_PIN.
#
# Re-vendor procedure (when bumping the pin, e.g. to b10331):
#
#   # 1. Resolve the commit for the new release tag:
#   gh api repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/refs/tags/b10331 --jq '.object.sha'
#
#   # 2. Fetch and unpack the source archive for that tag:
#   curl -fsSL -o /tmp/llama-src.tar.gz \
#     https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/archive/refs/tags/b10331.tar.gz
#   rm -rf /tmp/llama-src && mkdir /tmp/llama-src
#   tar -xzf /tmp/llama-src.tar.gz -C /tmp/llama-src
#   SRC=/tmp/llama-src/llama.cpp-b10331
#
#   # 3. Refresh the headers (DEST is the directory containing this file):
#   DEST=local-llm/Sources/CLlamaBridge/third_party/llama_cpp_common
#   cp "$SRC"/common/{chat,common,log,peg-parser}.h "$DEST/"
#   cp "$SRC"/common/{chat-peg-parser,chat-auto-parser,chat-auto-parser-helpers}.h "$DEST/"
#   cp "$SRC"/common/{json-schema-to-grammar,unicode}.h "$DEST/"
#   cp "$SRC"/common/jinja/*.h "$DEST/jinja/"
#   cp "$SRC"/vendor/nlohmann/{json,json_fwd}.hpp "$DEST/nlohmann/"
#
#   # 4. Re-vendor the public headers too, from the SAME tree — see
#   #    local-llm/third_party/llama_cpp_api/COMMIT
#
#   # 5. Compare the vendored set against upstream's common/ listing. Headers
#   #    get added and removed upstream: regex-partial.h was vendored here
#   #    through b9200 and no longer exists at b10330. If a file disappears
#   #    upstream, check nothing includes it, then `git rm` it.
#
#   # 6. Update the commit SHA above, in llama_cpp_api/COMMIT, and in
#   #    local-llm/LLAMA_CPP_PIN (LLAMA_CPP_COMMIT). provision-llama.sh fails
#   #    closed if the pin and the vendored headers disagree.
#
#   # 7. rm -rf .llama && ./scripts/provision-llama.sh
#   #    cd local-llm && swift test   — 21 tests, real inference; catches drift.
